{{define "title"}}Repeated failed sign-in attempts on your account{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hello{{if .Name}} {{.Name}}{{end}},</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">There were <strong>{{.Failures}}</strong> failed attempts against one of the
  ways you sign in to Chronos, so we have locked that method. This happened on
  <strong>{{datetime .OccurredAt}}</strong>.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Your account is <em>not</em> locked — only that one credential is, and your
  other ways in still work. That is deliberate: locking the whole account would let anyone who knows
  your address lock you out at will.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">If this wasn't you, somebody is guessing at your credentials.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
  <a href="{{url "/settings/security"}}" style="display:inline-block;background:#b42318;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;">Change your password</a>
</p>
{{end}}
